% SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2
% =====================================================================
% queries.clausal -- QUERY-COMBINATOR layer for uk/uk_pecr_cookie_exemptions_and_fines.
% A TOP-LAYER consumer: it imports the determination slice's PUBLIC
% predicates it calls, the kernel's input check (re-exported as the
% scaffold wrote it) and the provenance marker.
%
% Query types served (the drafter's reading, not a lawyer's):
%   #2  eligibility: decide_uk_pecr_cookie_exemptions_and_fines/2 and the
%       cited checklist live in the slice (the UK cookie verdict).
%   #5  comparison: compare_uk_eu_terminal_equipment_storage_or_access/5
%       lives in the slice.
%   #14 obligation surfacing: uk_pecr_cookie_exemptions_and_fines_obligations/2
%       (below) lists what the entity must do on the facts given.
%   #16 what-if: uk_pecr_cookie_exemptions_and_fines_what_if/4 re-decides
%       the cookie verdict with one key of the attribute list replaced.
%
% The profile is an ATTRIBUTE LIST [attribute(Key, Value), ...], so the
% what-if replaces the key in that list (the kit's dict override_key does
% not apply to an attribute list; the local replacement is plumbing).
%
% This module also owns the PACKAGE-ROOT VOCABULARY: the verdict atoms,
% the result constructors (data, no clauses), the thirty-three profile key
% atoms, the seventeen provision atoms, the judgement value unsure and the
% atom not_attempted, each exported so the facade carries it.
% =====================================================================

:- module(queries, [
    uk_pecr_cookie_exemptions_and_fines_profile_keys/1,
    uk_pecr_cookie_exemptions_and_fines_input_problems/2,
